      en: "Varėna Old Railway Station is a historic building from the late 19th century. It was built in 1899 as part of the Vilnius–Suwałki railway line. The station exemplifies typical railway architecture of the Russian Empire. It served as an important transport hub for passenger and freight traffic in the region. After closure in the 1990s, the building fell into disrepair. In the 2010s it was restored and converted into a cultural center and museum. The museum exhibits the history of railways in Lithuania. The station is a testament to the region's industrial development.",
